Carla Jean Moss, played by Kelly Macdonald.

10
00:45:11,111 --> 00:45:17,111
Wendell, played by Garret Dillahunt.

11
00:49:42,222 --> 00:49:48,222
No Country for Old Men is a 2007 American neo-Western crime thriller film written, directed,
produced, and edited by Joel and Ethan Coen, based on Cormac McCarthy's 2005 novel.

12
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:19,333
Starring Tommy Lee Jones, Javier Bardem, and Josh Brolin, the film is set
in the desert landscape of 1980 West Texas, United States.

13
00:58:44,444 --> 00:58:50,444
The film revisits the themes of fate, conscience, and circumstance that the Coen brothers had
explored in the films Blood Simple (1984), Raising Arizona (1987), and Fargo (1996).

14
01:03:15,555 --> 01:03:21,555
It follows three main characters: Llewelyn Moss (Brolin), a Vietnam War veteran and welder who stumbles upon a large sum of money in the desert,
Anton Chigurh (Bardem), a hitman who is sent to recover the money, and Ed Tom Bell (Jones), a sheriff investigating the crime.

15
01:07:46,666 --> 01:07:52,666
The film also stars Kelly Macdonald as Moss's wife, Carla Jean, and Woody Harrelson as
Carson Wells, a bounty hunter seeking Moss and the return of the money.

16
01:12:17,777 --> 01:12:23,777
No Country for Old Men premiered in competition at the
2007 Cannes Film Festival on May 19.

17
01:16:48,888 --> 01:16:54,888
The film became a commercial success, grossing $171 million
worldwide against a budget of $25 million.

18
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:26,000
Critics praised the Coens' direction and screenplay and Bardem's performance, and the film was heavily
awarded, winning four Academy Awards (including Best Picture), three BAFTAs, and two Golden Globes.

19
01:25:51,111 --> 01:25:57,111
The American Film Institute listed it as an AFI Movie of the Year, and the
National Board of Review selected it as the best of 2007.

20
01:30:22,222 --> 01:30:28,222
It is one of only four Western films ever to win the Academy Award for Best Picture (the others
being Cimarron in 1931, Dances with Wolves in 1990, and Unforgiven in 1992).

21
01:34:53,333 --> 01:34:59,333
No Country for Old Men was considered one of the best films of 2007,
and many regard it as the Coen brothers' magnum opus.

22
01:39:24,444 --> 01:39:30,444
It has since been widely recognized as one of the
greatest films of the 2000s and 21st century.

23
01:43:55,555 --> 01:44:01,555
The Guardian's John Patterson wrote: "the Coens' technical abilities, and their feel for a landscape-based Western classicism reminiscent of Anthony Mann and Sam Peckinpah, are
matched by few living directors", and Peter Travers of Rolling Stone said that it is "a new career peak for the Coen brothers" and "as entertaining as hell".

24
01:48:26,666 --> 01:48:32,666
In 2024, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

25
01:52:57,777 --> 01:53:03,777
The film explores themes of vietnam veteran, sheriff,
trailer park, based on novel or book, hitman.

26
